\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"198.502702\" y=\"29.637931\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"214.228156\" y=\"20.948276\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"229.953611\" y=\"15.051724\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"245.679065\" y=\"13.5\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"261.40452\" y=\"16.603448\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"277.129974\" y=\"24.982759\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"292.855429\" y=\"38.017241\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"308.580884\" y=\"54.775862\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"324.306338\" y=\"74.017241\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"340.031793\" y=\"95.12069\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"355.757247\" y=\"117.155172\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#m0d64a9a55a\" x=\"371.482702\" y=\"139.5\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c; stroke: #0a8f9c\"/></g></g><g id=\"patch_3\"><path d=\"M 41.248156 145.8 L 41.248156 7.2 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_4\"><path d=\"M 41.248156 145.8 L 387.208156 145.8 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pd5b1738dee\"><rect x=\"41.248156\" y=\"7.2\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"138.6\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Expected profit by extra bookings accepted","note":null},"answer":"<p>Expected profit peaks at about <b>24 extra bookings</b>: $60,435 a night, against $56,580 with no overbooking: about $3,855 more a night.</p> <p>At 24, the hotel expects to walk about 1.1 guests a night; at 26 it would walk about 1.9 and earn less ($60,330).</p>","note":"Assumes each booked guest independently has a 92% chance of arriving."},{"q":"How would you make overbooking safer?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li>Overbook less on nights with many loyalty members or conference speakers, who must not be walked</li><li>Charge no-shows on more rates, which lowers the no-show rate itself</li> <li>Agree a standing arrangement with a nearby hotel, and always walk guests to a better hotel with a clear apology</li><li>Update no-show estimates by day, season and booking source</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Accept about 24 bookings beyond the 300 rooms on busy weeknights. That's a little fewer than the 26 needed to expect a full house, because walking a guest ($400) costs nearly twice what a room earns ($205). It raises expected profit by about $3,855 a night, with about 1.1 guests a night walked on average. Protect loyalty members and VIPs from being walked, and keep an agreement with a nearby hotel. Next step: estimate no-show rates by booking source and day of week.","great":["Explains why the best level is below the bookings that would fill the hotel on average","Weighs the margin of a filled room against the cost of walking a guest","Reads the expected-profit curve","Protects the most valuable guests"],"id":98,"slug":"alder-grand-hotel"}